-- title:
--   MIP* = RE for the computable class, given an answer reduction stage
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be an answer reduction stage for $5$-level normal form verifiers (`MIPRE.AnswerReduction 5`). For a language $L$, a set of bit strings, `IsRE L` (blueprint `def:re`) says that membership in $L$ is the domain of a partial computable function, and `MIPStarComputable L` (blueprint `def:mipstar-computable`) says that there is a computable map $g$ from bit strings to game descriptions such that the game $(g\,x).\mathrm{game}$ has quantum value $1$ for $x \in L$ and at most $\tfrac12$ for $x \notin L$. Then the two predicates on languages coincide:
--
--   $$ \mathrm{MIPStarComputable} \;=\; \mathrm{IsRE} \qquad \text{as predicates on } \mathcal{P}(\{0,1\}^*). $$
--
--   This is blueprint `thm:mipstar-eq-re` for the computable class of `def:mipstar-computable`, with the single remaining hypothesis an `AnswerReduction 5`: introspection, parallel repetition and the universal machine are supplied. The inclusion $\mathrm{MIP}^* \subseteq \mathrm{RE}$ is `MIPStarComputable.isRE` (blueprint `lem:value-lower-approx` at the threshold $\tfrac12$) and needs no hypothesis; the reverse inclusion is `re_subset_mipstarComputable_of_answerReduction`.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is an equality of functions `Set BitStr → Prop`, `MIPStarComputable = IsRE`, equivalent by function and propositional extensionality to `∀ L, MIPStarComputable L ↔ IsRE L`. `IsRE L := REPred (· ∈ L)` and `MIPStarComputable L := ∃ g : BitStr → GameData, Computable g ∧ ∀ x, (x ∈ L → quantumValue (g x).game = 1) ∧ (x ∉ L → quantumValue (g x).game ≤ 1 / 2)`, with `BitStr = List Bool` and `1 / 2 : ℝ`. The hypothesis `A : MIPRE.AnswerReduction 5` is an explicit argument. `GapCompression.ofAnswerReduction A := GapCompression.ofPipeline Introspection.seven A (repetition 7)` (same file) is the compression theorem built from the supplied introspection and repetition stages, of which this is the conditional consequence. Namespace `MIPRE.Halting`, file `MIPRE/Background/Pipeline.lean`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/vidick/MIPRE-formalization/blob/70cbf1c52e3d5e1dff1162fdf952c9a9f4bd99ed/MIPRE/Background/Pipeline.lean#L91-L92; blueprint cor:compression-from-answer-reduction

